  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-12), moved from the earlier photo",
  "mappingSource": "the sheet itself (Virpil support \"VPC SharKa-50 Control Panel\", https://support.virpil.com/en/support/solutions/articles/47001250817-vpc-sharka-50-control-panel, attachment 47246732690). The sheet draws one leader line per box group and chains the dots of a group (e.g. one line through all keys of a keypad), so the number of each control inside a group comes from the box arrangement, which mirrors the physical arrangement",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "product render straight from above/front, levers along the back (top of the photo). Every control of the sheet is visible and printed-label matched: levers X, Y, rX, rY left to right; keypad B1 B2 / B3 B4 = 1 2 / 6 7; START, APU, STOP = 3, 4, 5; LH ENG/RH ENG toggle 9/8; START/CRANK 10/11; MASTER ARM 12/13; HMS, AUTO/TS, LAS toggles 14/15, 16/17, 18/19; keypad RST B5 B6 DIP = 20 21 22 23, B7 B8 = 27 28; BRT knob 24-26, right knob 29-31; MODE selector 32-36; MAN/AUTO 37/38, LNG/MD/SHORT 39-41, HE/API 42/43, LOW/HIGH 44/45. Which lever position/selector position is which number inside a toggle group is not drawn; all positions of one control sit on that control.",
